     I think it was Dylan who first pointed out that it's even
simpler than that:  skip the middle third of #1 (no need for
any scrolls); for the second half of turn #2, wish for an altar
of your alignment, making that actually be the second third of
turn #2 since no time elapses.  Then for third third of turn #2,
#offer.

     A side-effect of some offering changes has made--or will
make, from your perspective--the shorter method impossible in
whatever future version may eventually appear.  Offering any
amulet on an altar which is not a high altar will only produce
a message.  And it is not possible to wish for a high altar.
(Don't worry; a high altar remains such even if the attending
high priest has been killed.)


